      "content": "There is no single objective consensus that the TPP definitively \"hurt\" all blue-collar work, as the outcomes were highly varied by industry and region.\n\nThe argument for harm primarily comes from union and progressive advocacy groups, who point to the potential for \"race to the bottom\" on labor and environmental standards in the pursuit of lower trade barriers.\n\nConversely, supporters argue that the gains in overall economic stability and certain high-demand, advanced manufacturing sectors would ultimately benefit the broader working class, making it a highly partisan issue rather than a clear-cut statistical outcome for all blue-collar jobs.",
