      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's partisan, but it feels like you're treating both sides as equally valid when the actual data on job losses in manufacturing is pretty damning. if you look at the actual economic reality for workers in the rust belt, isn't it more accurate to say the TPP was fundamentally a failure for them? wouldn't saying \"both sides have points\" just be ignoring the lived experience of people who lost their livelihoods?",
